.TH GIT-VET 1
.SH NAME
git-vet \- track review state for Git-tracked file contents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git vet
[\fB\-\-channel\fR \fICHANNEL\fR]
[\fB\-\-color\fR \fIWHEN\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B git-vet
[\fB\-\-channel\fR \fICHANNEL\fR]
[\fB\-\-color\fR \fIWHEN\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-vet
records that the exact contents of a tracked file have been reviewed.
Review state is keyed by Git blob object ID, so changing a file creates content
that must be reviewed again.
.PP
State is stored per review channel in
.BR refs/notes/vet/<channel> .
The selected channel comes from
.BR \-\-channel ,
then
.BR vet.channel ,
and otherwise defaults to
.BR default .
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-channel " CHANNEL"
Use the named review channel. Channel names are flat and cannot contain a slash.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " WHEN"
Control colored output. Values are
.BR auto ,
.BR always ,
and
.BR never .
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Print command-line help. When invoked through Git, use
.B git vet \-h
for concise command-line help; Git reserves
.B git vet \-\-help
for this manual page.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Print the version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install-man
[\fB\-\-man-dir\fR \fIDIRECTORY\fR]
Install this manual as
.B git-vet.1
in a user man-page directory. The default is
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/man/man1
when
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
is set, otherwise
.IR $HOME/.local/share/man/man1 .
This command does not require a Git repository.
.TP
.B channel list
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
List local review-note channels.
.TP
.B channel copy
.I SOURCE DESTINATION
Copy all local review notes from an existing channel into a new channel.
.TP
.B channel move
.I SOURCE DESTINATION
Move all local review notes from an existing channel to a new channel.
.TP
.B channel remove
.I CHANNEL
[\fB\-\-force\fR]
Delete a local review-note channel. Non-interactive use requires
.BR \-\-force .
.TP
.B mark
[\fB\-\-allow-dirty\fR]
.I PATH...
Mark each path's current committed HEAD content as reviewed. Dirty target paths
require confirmation unless
.B \-\-allow-dirty
is supplied; only committed content is marked in either case.
.TP
.B unmark
.I PATH...
Remove review state from each path's current committed HEAD content. Paths with
identical contents share blob-keyed state.
.TP
.B status
[\fB\-\-workspace\fR]
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
[\fB\-\-all\fR]
[\fB\-\-check\fR]
[\fIPATHSPEC...\fR]
Classify selected tracked files as
.BR vetted ,
.BR stale ,
or
.BR new .
With
.BR \-\-workspace ,
classify working-tree contents instead of HEAD. With
.BR \-\-check ,
exit 1 if any selected file is not reviewed.
.TP
.B diff
[\fB\-\-workspace\fR]
.I PATH
Show the change that remains to be reviewed, from the latest reviewed version
(or an empty file) to HEAD. With
.BR \-\-workspace ,
use working-tree content as the target.
.TP
.B sync
[\fB\-\-remote\fR \fIREMOTE\fR]
Fetch, merge, and push the selected channel's notes. Remote selection uses the
explicit option, then
.BR vet.syncRemote ,
then
.BR origin .
.TP
.B prune
Prune notes for objects that no longer exist.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B .vetignore
Gitignore-style patterns excluded in every channel.
.TP
.BI .vetignore. CHANNEL
Additional Gitignore-style patterns for one channel.
.TP
.BI refs/notes/vet/ CHANNEL
Git notes ref containing the channel's blob-keyed review records.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command succeeded, or
.B status --check
found every selected file reviewed.
.TP
.B 1
.B status --check
found one or more unreviewed files.
.TP
.B 2
A usage or runtime error occurred.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
git vet status
git vet diff src/lib.rs
git vet mark src/lib.rs
git vet status --check
git vet --channel security status
git vet sync --remote origin
git-vet install-man
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-notes (1),
.BR git-diff (1)
